; A reference journal for `hledger-x fmt --explicit`.
;
; Every case --explicit changes, and the notable ones it deliberately leaves
; alone. The file is valid hledger, so the two can be compared directly:
;
;   hledger-x fmt --explicit --diff tests/golden/explicit.in.ledger
;   hledger print -x -f tests/golden/explicit.in.ledger
;
; Accounts are namespaced per transaction so every balance assertion stands on
; its own and any case can be reordered or deleted on its own.

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Declared commodity styles. Only a *declared* style enables decimal padding;
; a commodity with no directive is never padded.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

commodity 1,000.00 EUR
commodity $1,000.00
commodity 1_000.00 SEK
commodity CHF
    format 1,000.000 CHF
D 1,000.00 GBP

commodity 1 000.00 USD

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Filling in the amount hledger would infer.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

2026-01-01 one posting left blank
    ; the classic case: the remainder is worked out and written in
    t01:expenses  1234 EUR
    t01:assets

2026-01-02 inferred through a unit cost
    ; the cost side is what balances, so the blank posting gets EUR
    t02:broker  10 CHF @ 1.1 EUR
    t02:assets

2026-01-03 inferred through a total cost
    t03:broker  10 CHF @@ 11 EUR
    t03:assets

2026-01-04 a posting carrying only a balance assertion
    ; the amount goes in front of the assertion, which is left alone
    t04:expenses  10 EUR
    t04:assets   = -10 EUR

2026-01-05 all four assertion operators
    ; =, ==, =* and ==* all leave the posting's contribution alone
    t05:a  10 EUR = 10 EUR
    t05:b  10 EUR == 10 EUR
    t05:c  10 EUR =* 10 EUR
    t05:d  10 EUR ==* 10 EUR
    t05:equity

2026-01-06 a cost with its amount attached
    ; `@1.1EUR` is one token, not three
    t06:broker  10 CHF @1.1EUR
    t06:assets

2026-01-07 an assertion with its amount attached
    t07:expenses  10 EUR
    t07:assets  -10 EUR =-10EUR

2026-01-08 everything already balances
    ; the remainder is zero, and an explicit zero is still written
    t08:expenses   10 EUR
    t08:assets    -10 EUR
    t08:rounding

2026-01-09 a remainder spanning two commodities
    ; the blank posting becomes one posting per commodity
    t09:broker  10 EUR
    t09:broker  10 GBP
    t09:assets

2026-01-10 the three posting kinds balance separately
    ; (...) contributes to nothing; [...] balances among its own kind
    t10:expenses  10 EUR
    (t10:budget)  10 EUR
    t10:assets
    [t10:tracked]  4 EUR
    [t10:mirror]

2026-01-11 unitless amounts stay unitless
    ; a commodity is never inferred, so the filled-in amount has none either.
    ; note that the `D` directive above makes hledger *read* a bare amount as
    ; GBP — that is hledger applying a default, not hledger-x writing one
    t11:steps  10000
    t11:balance

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Padding to the commodity's declared decimal places. `fmt` on its own never
; does this — it is the second half of what --explicit means.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

2026-02-01 a declared right-side style
    t21:expenses   1234 EUR
    t21:assets    -1234 EUR

2026-02-02 a declared attached-left style
    t22:expenses  $1234
    t22:assets    $-1234

2026-02-03 the sign written before the symbol
    ; `-$1234` and `$-1234` are one commodity, and both render hledger's way
    t23:expenses  -$1234
    t23:assets    $1234

2026-02-04 an underscore as the digit group mark
    t24:expenses   1234 SEK
    t24:assets    -1234 SEK

2026-02-05 a style declared by a `format` subdirective
    t25:expenses   1234 CHF
    t25:assets    -1234 CHF

2026-02-06 a style declared by `D`
    t26:expenses   1234 GBP
    t26:assets    -1234 GBP

2026-02-07 costs and assertions are padded too
    ; both sides of the `@`, and the assertion's own amount
    t27:broker  10 CHF @ 1.1 EUR
    t27:assets  -11 EUR = -11 EUR

2026-02-09 a space as the digit group mark
    ; a space between digit groups is part of the number, not the boundary
    ; with the commodity — `1 234.00 USD` is one amount
    t29:expenses   1234567 USD
    t29:assets    -1234567 USD

2026-02-10 a space-grouped amount already in the journal
    ; and it lines up with an ungrouped one in the same column
    t30:expenses   1 234.00 USD
    t30:assets       -50.00 USD
    t30:rest

2026-02-08 more precision than declared is kept
    ; the declared places are a floor, never a ceiling: rounding would lose
    ; value, so 4.0001 is left exactly as written
    t28:expenses   4.0001 EUR
    t28:assets    -4.0001 EUR

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Commodities with no directive. Nothing is padded — but an amount that has to
; be *generated* still has to be written somehow, and it copies the posting it
; balances against.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

2026-03-01 undeclared, symbol on the right with a space
    t31:crypto  0.5 BTC
    t31:equity

2026-03-02 undeclared, symbol attached on the left
    t32:expenses  Kc10
    t32:assets

2026-03-03 undeclared, symbol attached on the right
    t33:expenses  10sat
    t33:assets

2026-03-04 undeclared, symbol first
    t34:expenses  NOK 10
    t34:assets

2026-03-05 typed digit grouping is carried into the generated amount
    t35:expenses  1,234.50 JPY
    t35:assets

2026-03-06 the style may come from a cost tail rather than a face
    t36:broker  10 DKK @ Kc1.1
    t36:assets

2026-03-07 a unitless amount keeps the grouping it was written with
    ; no commodity to declare a style, so the sibling's own notation is
    ; copied — answering `1 000` with a bare `-1000` read as badly as
    ; answering `$10` with `-10 $`
    t37:steps  1 000
    t37:balance

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Deliberately left alone.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

2026-04-01 an undeclared commodity is never padded
    ; `1 PLN` stays `1 PLN`; only a declared style says what "filled out" means
    t41:expenses   1 PLN
    t41:assets    -1 PLN

2026-04-02 lot notation is not understood
    ; hledger would fill `$-50` here from the lot cost. hledger-x cannot read
    ; `{...}`, so the amount does not parse and the whole transaction is left
    ; as it stands rather than guessed at
    t42:shares  10 AAPL {$5}
    t42:cash

~ monthly  rent
    ; a periodic rule is not a transaction, and is never touched
    t51:expenses  1234 EUR
    t51:assets

= t52:expenses
    ; an auto-posting rule is not a transaction either, and its `*2`
    ; multiplier is not an amount
    (t52:budget)  *2

comment
A comment block is prose, not journal syntax. Nothing in here is filled in,
padded or aligned, even though it looks exactly like a transaction:

2026-09-09 not a transaction
    a  1234 EUR
    b
end comment
